[37m[100m❯ [97mList five common git subcommands, one line each with a short description. Do not use any tools.[39m

[97m[49m⏺[39m Aye, captain, here are five common ones:

  - [94mgit status[39m: shows which files are changed, staged, or untracked in the working tree.
  - [94mgit add[39m: stages changes so they go into the next commit.
  - [94mgit commit[39m: saves the staged changes as a new commit, with a message.
  - [94mgit log[39m: lists the commit history for the current branch.
  - [94mgit push[39m: uploads your local commits to a remote repository.

